side organizations  to change a culture of silence  so what are you trying to do to bring  about real change how do you do that  well we've done a number of things and  and particularly as it relates to  accountability  uh one of the measures we're introducing  is a new platform that will allow for  greater accountability it's a tech  enabled platform  that allows for an individual  to  log on to an app that they will be  provided  by an organization with with their  associated  whether it's a studio or a guild  and they can report problems that  are occurring in their workplaces you  know the battle for equality in the  entertainment industry  sort of seems to mirror what's going on  in social justice right now as well  don't you think  absolutely the issue of accountability  is not limited to  hollywood it's not limited to issues of  of sexual harassment  the issues of accountability process  movements like black lives matter people  want  accountability for the deaths of brianna  taylor  uh and george floyd people want  accountability for  where we are right now in in with covet  and the issues that people are facing  with their help  yeah yeah i wanted to talk to i wanted  it's bigger than any one survey can  capture but we've  definitely worked hard to understand  where workers are with the issue of  accountability and what they want  in order to solve the problem i hear  that i wanted to talk now to private  citizen anita hill is she available  maybe she's wearing different glasses is  she there  should i change my glasses yeah i'd like  to yes i'd like to talk to private  citizen anita hill if you don't mind  because because she said that  you're absolutely not convinced that a  thorough supreme court confirmation can  happen  before the election why do you think  that  people are concerned about  uh so many things that are going on  but to start with just let's let's think  about what a confirmation hearing  is there for it's there for the senate  to underst